NixMount provides the functionality of two earlier projects:

  Ext4Fsd, by Matt Wu, Bo Branten and contributors (GPL-2.0)
  https://github.com/bobranten/Ext4Fsd

  WinBtrfs, by Mark Harmstone (LGPL-3.0)
  https://github.com/maharmstone/btrfs

NixMount is new code written against the documented on-disk formats of ext4, jbd2 and
Btrfs. No source file from either project was copied or translated. This matters because
GPL-2.0-only and LGPL-3.0 code cannot be combined in one program. GPL-2.0 was chosen so that
NixMount stays compatible with Ext4Fsd, the project it most directly replaces.

WinFsp is used under its FLOSS exception, which permits linking with its DLL and distributing
its unmodified installer. app/res holds the official, signed installer, unchanged, and the
executable carries it for setup. The DLL is loaded at run time from where that installer puts it.

  WinFsp - Windows File System Proxy, Copyright (C) Bill Zissimopoulos
  https://github.com/winfsp/winfsp

LUKS support is new code written against the LUKS1 and LUKS2 specifications. Three test
images in tests/fixtures/cryptsetup come from cryptsetup's own test suite (GPL-2.0-or-later),
re-compressed and renamed, and are only used by tests:

  cryptsetup, by Clemens Fruhwirth, Milan Broz and contributors
  https://gitlab.com/cryptsetup/cryptsetup

Third-party Rust crates are used under their own permissive licenses, all compatible with
GPL-2.0: see Cargo.lock for the list.
